{
  "_README": [
    "R12/R13 \u2014 libretto speaker labels that do not match any stave name.",
    "EVERY MAPPING IN HERE IS A GUESS BY THE TOOL AND IS MEANT TO BE CORRECTED.",
    "",
    "Values:",
    "  [\"Soprano\", \"Alto\"]  -> this body sings those voice parts",
    "  \"*create*\"           -> a named character the archive never gave a stave;",
    "  \"*principal:Soprano*\" -> R5: a chorus member who steps out for a line and",
    "                          returns. Gets a FULL-LENGTH stave copied from that",
    "                          chorus voice; their solo text is placed where the",
    "                          libretto attributes it, chorus text elsewhere.",
    "                          The voice named after the colon is a GUESS.",
    "                          R13 builds one from the lyric-crib notes",
    "  \"*rest*\"             -> contextual ('OTHERS', 'ALL FOUR'): resolved at",
    "                          run time to whoever is sounding and not already",
    "                          named in that passage",
    "  \"*ignore*\"           -> not a speaker; a parse artefact",
    "",
    "",
    "CHORUS BODIES: a dramatic body ('Bridesmaids', 'Peers', 'Fairies') is split",
    "into VOICE PARTS, because a chorister picks their voice once and needs it in",
    "every number \u2014 naming staves after the body would fragment that and 'Soprano'",
    "would appear nowhere. Unison passages carry the same notes in each stave, so",
    "either selection still plays the number.",
    "",
    "EVERY ENTRY BELOW IS A GUESS. They are voiced from the plot, not the music."
  ],
